WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.871
ALEX: So. One billion dollars. AMD
takes a one-billion-dollar

00:00:02.871 --> 00:00:05.743
ALEX: quarterly charge tied to its
AI chip supply

00:00:05.743 --> 00:00:08.614
ALEX: agreements with OpenAI and
Meta. Reuters has this.

00:00:08.614 --> 00:00:11.485
ALEX: And I want to get the
accounting right,

00:00:11.485 --> 00:00:14.357
ALEX: because a charge isn't the
same as losing

00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:17.228
ALEX: a billion dollars outright,
is it?

00:00:17.313 --> 00:00:19.362
JAMIE: And it's specifically the
OpenAI and Meta deals.

00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:21.410
JAMIE: Not general overhead. This
is the price of

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.459
JAMIE: being their chipmaker.

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:25.908
ALEX: So AMD locked in these
agreements, committed to

00:00:25.908 --> 00:00:28.247
ALEX: supplying at a certain
scale, and the accounting

00:00:28.247 --> 00:00:30.586
ALEX: weight of that lands as a
billion-dollar hit

00:00:30.586 --> 00:00:32.925
ALEX: in a single quarter.
